  "answer": "You can customize the response status code of a FastAPI endpoint by using the `Response` object and setting the `status_code` attribute. For example: \n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import Response\n\nasync def endpoint():\n    return Response(\"Hello\", status_code=202)\n```\n\nAlternatively, you can use the `Response` object with a dictionary to set the status code and other response headers. \n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import Response\n\nasync def endpoint():\n    return Response({\"message\": \"Hello\"}, status_code=202)\n```",
